---
import beforeTranslating from "../../captures/before-translating.png";
import seriesLanguages from "../../captures/series-languages.png";
import textRecognition from "../../captures/text-recognition.png";
import translationAfter from "../../captures/translation-after.png";
import translationEngines from "../../captures/translation-engines.png";
import translationPopup from "../../captures/translation-popup.png";
import translator from "../../captures/translator.png";
import Callout from "../../guide/Callout.astro";
import GuidePage from "../../guide/GuidePage.astro";
import Path from "../../guide/Path.astro";
import Task from "../../guide/Task.astro";
---

<GuidePage
  slug="translation"
  lead="Katari finds the text on a comic page and translates it. Text recognition always runs on the phone; with the right engine, translation does too."
>
  <Task id="engine" title="Pick a translation engine" shot={{ image: translationEngines, alt: "The translation engines, each saying whether it is ready", caption: "Translation engine" }}>
    <p>
      Under <strong>Playground</strong> in <Path>Settings › Translation</Path>, tap the engine's name to pick another under <strong>Translation engine</strong>, and
      the language on the right to choose the one to translate into. Tap <strong>Save</strong> to keep them.
    </p>
    <table class="terms">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Engine</th> <th>Runs</th> <th>What it needs</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Android System Translation</strong></td> <td data-label="Runs">On the phone</td> <td data-label="Needs">Android 12 or newer</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Offline Translator</strong></td> <td data-label="Runs">On the phone</td> <td data-label="Needs">The Offline Translator app, set up as below</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>DeepL-compatible server</strong></td> <td data-label="Runs">Over the network</td> <td data-label="Needs">For DeepL, an API key, with <strong>DeepL API Free</strong> or <strong>DeepL API Pro</strong> picked as the server; for a server of your own, its URL</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>LibreTranslate Server</strong></td> <td data-label="Runs">Over the network</td> <td data-label="Needs">A server URL, and an API key if the server asks</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>To try the engine, type in the box under its name.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="offline-translator" title="Set up Offline Translator">
    <ol>
      <li>Install Offline Translator from F-Droid and download its language models.</li>
      <li>In Offline Translator, turn on its HTTP API and limit it to localhost, so only apps on this phone can reach it.</li>
      <li>In Katari, pick <strong>Offline Translator</strong> as the engine, confirm the <strong>HTTP API port</strong> (5000 unless you changed it), and tap <strong>Test connection</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
  </Task>

  <Task id="page" title="Translate a comic page" shot={{ image: translationAfter, alt: "A comic page with its speech bubbles translated into English", caption: "Translations on the page" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>In the reader, tap the translate button in the bottom bar. A translation bar opens.</li>
      <li>
        The first time, the bar asks what it needs: <strong>Which language is the text in?</strong>, how to read that language, and the
        models to download. Answer each with its button.
      </li>
      <li>Once the bar shows the page's languages, such as Japanese → English, tap a speech bubble.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The subtitles button in the bar draws every bubble's translation over the page. The selection button beside it translates text
      you drag over, for writing outside the bubbles.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="bubble" title="Hear a bubble read aloud" shot={{ image: translationPopup, alt: "One speech bubble's translation with buttons to hear it read aloud", caption: "One bubble" }}>
    <p>
      A tapped bubble shows its translation beside the original. The speaker beside each language reads that one aloud with the phone's
      text-to-speech voices.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pick the speech engine, the voice and its pitch under <Path>Settings › Text to speech</Path>, and hear them with <strong>Play preview</strong>. A voice
      that runs over the network asks first, with <strong>Use network voice?</strong>
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="text-recognition" title="Choose how text is recognized" shot={{ image: textRecognition, alt: "Text recognition models by language, with Japanese downloaded and the rest still to download", caption: "Languages" }}>
    <p>Katari reads the page with models it downloads once and keeps on the phone. The bar picks them by the page's language:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Japanese manga</strong> reads Japanese, vertical text and furigana included.</li>
      <li>Other languages have their own option, such as <strong>Korean comics</strong> or <strong>Cyrillic comics</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Comics with ML Kit</strong> uses Google's text recognition instead. It reads vertical text less reliably.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <Path>Settings › Text recognition</Path> changes the engine and the choice per language, lists <strong>Downloaded models</strong> with
      their size, and has a playground for trying a picture.
    </p>
    <Callout label="Mobile data" tone="warning">
      <p>
        Models only download over Wi-Fi or another unmetered network unless you tick <strong>Allow download over mobile data</strong> in
        <strong>Download models?</strong> Otherwise the download stops at <strong>Waiting for a non-metered network</strong>; start it again
        with the box ticked, or on Wi-Fi.
      </p>
    </Callout>
    <Callout label="Katari FOSS">
      <p>ML Kit needs Google Play services, so Katari FOSS leaves it out. Every other option works in both.</p>
    </Callout>
  </Task>

  <Task id="series" title="Keep a series' languages" shot={{ image: seriesLanguages, alt: "A series' page language and target language, over its translated page", caption: "Languages for this series" }}>
    <p>
      Tap the language chip in the translation bar to open <strong>Languages for this series</strong>. <strong>Page language</strong> and
      <strong>Translate to</strong> stay with the series. After you change the page language, Katari reads its pages again. <strong>Translate downloads</strong>
      translates the series' chapters in the background once they're downloaded. In a merged entry, each member keeps its own languages.
    </p>
    <p>
      <Path>Settings › Translation › Series languages</Path> lists every series with its own languages, where you can return one or all of
      them to the defaults.
    </p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="chapters" title="Translate whole chapters ahead" shot={{ image: beforeTranslating, alt: "What a chapter still needs before it can be translated, each with a button to fix it", caption: "Before translating" }}>
    <ol>
      <li>On a title's page, long-press chapters to select them and tap <strong>Translate</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Before translating</strong> lists anything still missing, each with a button to fix it. Then tap <strong>Translate</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Under <Path>Settings › Downloads › Auto-translate</Path>, Katari can translate downloaded chapters by itself, as they arrive and
      ahead of the one you're reading:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Translate new items</strong> works together with <strong>Download new items</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Translate ahead while viewing</strong>, off at first, translates the next 2 to 10 unread chapters once they're downloaded.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Only on Wi-Fi</strong>, on from the start, holds back engines that work over the network; <strong>Only while charging</strong> is off.</li>
    </ul>
  </Task>

  <Task id="translator" title="Translate typed text" shot={{ image: translator, alt: "The Translator turning a line of Japanese into English", caption: "The Translator" }}>
    <p>
      The <strong>Translator</strong> tab translates anything you type or paste, with <strong>Detect language</strong> for text you can't
      place. It is hidden at first; add it under <Path>Settings › Appearance › Home screen tabs</Path>.
    </p>
    <p>In books, select text to get <strong>Copy</strong>, <strong>Listen</strong> and <strong>Translate</strong> for that passage.</p>
  </Task>

  <Task id="backups" title="What carries over to another phone">
    <p>
      Backups keep the engine, target language, voices and text recognition choices with each profile. They leave out server addresses
      and API keys, which stay on this phone, and the models, which download again when a page needs them.
    </p>
  </Task>
</GuidePage>
